{
  "table_id": "Table_S13",
  "display_number": "S13",
  "title": "Supplementary Table S13. Predictive scenario contrasts by age and exposure pattern",
  "panel": "",
  "panel_title": "",
  "notes_before": [],
  "notes_after": [
    "Note. Age-stratified predicted BAA reductions (current prediction minus joint-scenario prediction; positive values indicate lower predicted BAA under the scenario) were estimated from the LightGBM model by setting adverse exposure values to target levels (EVI < 0.40 → 0.40; O₃ > 60 μg m⁻³ → 60 μg m⁻³). Rows are exposure-eligibility patterns: Both exposures adverse = EVI < 0.40 and O₃ > 60 μg m⁻³; Only O₃ adverse = EVI ≥ 0.40 and O₃ > 60 μg m⁻³ (no participant had only adverse EVI). In the analytic sample (N = 5,914), mean predicted BAA differences (scenario minus current) were −0.39 years (EVI-only scenario), −0.34 years (O₃-only scenario) and −0.63 years (joint scenario). The model had negligible held-out explained variance (R² = 0.0045); these scenario contrasts are descriptive model outputs and do not estimate causal intervention effects. A participant-level re-evaluation found no out-of-sample predictive skill (held-out test R² = -0.013; Supplementary Note on predictive analyses and Supplementary Table S30).",
    "Abbreviations: BAA, biological age acceleration; CI, confidence interval; EVI, enhanced vegetation index; O₃, ozone; SE, standard error."
  ],
